msgid ""
"Scheduler load ( default 20 )- This value can be between 1 and 100. A scheduler "
"load of 20 implies that 20% of CPU is used for indexing. This is calculated "
"based on time taken for last index job. Say the last index job took 20secs. The "
"next index job is scheduled to resume after 80secs.( this is wait time )"
msgstr ""

#: katcontrol/katcontrol.cpp:392
msgid "Wait in seconds before next scheduler job:"
msgstr ""

#: katcontrol/katcontrol.cpp:395
msgid "s"
msgstr "s"

#: katcontrol/katcontrol.cpp:397
msgid ""
"Scheduler maximum wait time  ( 120 secs. ) - Schedule the next job no later "
"than this. Say the previous job took 60secs. the next job will scheduled after "
"240secs. This introduces considerable delay and so we limit that so as not to "
"let the index time lag."
msgstr ""

